// Rule: [T1102.002][T1071.001] Hollowgraph - Hollowgraph Future Calendar Access
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1102.002, T1071.001
// Classification: Hunting query
// Status: Hunting query
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR
// Required telemetry: MicrosoftGraphActivityLogs
// Purpose: Generalized Microsoft Graph discovery experiment for calendarView ranges in years 2040-2099.
// Logic: Evaluate MicrosoftGraphActivityLogs for hollowgraph future calendar access using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: A match indicates a calendarView request targeting a year from 2040 through 2099.
// A match does not prove: HOLLOWGRAPH, covert tasking, malicious attachment access or compromised credentials.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// Title: Far-future Microsoft Graph calendarView access
// Status: Hunting query
// Confidence: High for telemetry observability; Medium for maliciousness
// Purpose: Identify calendarView requests whose startDateTime targets years
//          2040-2099, generalizing the far-future calendar behavior observed
//          in HOLLOWGRAPH.
// Required table: MicrosoftGraphActivityLogs
// Required fields: TimeGenerated, RequestMethod, RequestUri,
//                  ResponseStatusCode, AppId, ServicePrincipalId, UserId,
//                  IPAddress, UserAgent
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1102.002, T1071.001
//
// This query must not be promoted directly to a production rule. First
// establish which approved applications legitimately query far-future dates.
// The regex assumes RequestUri retains a readable startDateTime parameter.

MicrosoftGraphActivityLogs
| where TimeGenerated >= ago(30d)
| where RequestMethod == "GET"
| where RequestUri contains "/calendarView"
| where RequestUri matches regex @"(?i)[?&]startDateTime=20[4-9][0-9]-"
| project
    TimeGenerated,
    AppId,
    ServicePrincipalId,
    UserId,
    IPAddress,
    UserAgent,
    RequestUri,
    ResponseStatusCode
